26-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp (listing /en-US/land/colorado-cortez-rv-resort-7rvhowjx)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Montezuma County, 14 mi from Mancos on Hipcamp: a \"35-site resort with diverse lodging near Mesa Verde National Park and regional attractions\"."},{"name":"Mancos State Park","source":"https://cpw.state.co.us/state-parks/mancos-state-park","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"cpwshop.com or 1-800-244-5613","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Colorado Parks and Wildlife: \"an ideal destination for outdoor enthusiasts and travelers year-round\"; 32 campsites; open daily 5 a.m. to 10 p.m.; reservations at cpwshop.com or 1-800-244-5613."},{"name":"Bright Star Campground","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/d/united-states/colorado/mancos/camping/glamping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","glamping","culture"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp (listing /en-US/land/colorado-bright-star-campground-g1xmhz12)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"Montezuma County, 11 mi from Mancos: a \"Community-driven campground with tipis, camping cabins, tent/RV sites, and a Navajo Hogan\"; \"complimentary WiFi, drinking water, ice, hot showers.\""},{"name":"The Dome at Mesa Verde","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/d/united-states/colorado/mancos/camping/glamping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp (listing /en-US/land/colorado-the-dome-at-mesa-verde-pw1h6eyn)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"Montezuma County, 9.5 mi from Mancos: a \"Luxury custom geodesic dome on 250 acres with sauna, firepit\" and \"on-site Concierge\" services (Hipcamp listing summary; the listing page itself did not render)."},{"name":"Southwest Luxury Glamping","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/d/united-states/colorado/mancos/camping/glamping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp (listing /en-US/land/colorado-southwest-luxury-glamping-ozxhz7dn)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"Montezuma County, 1.8 mi from Mancos: \"Three glamping sites minutes from downtown Mancos with proximity to Mesa Verde.\""},{"name":"Canyon Trails Ranch","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/d/united-states/colorado/mancos/camping/glamping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp (listing /en-US/land/colorado-canyon-trails-ranch-1xmho8v9)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"Montezuma County, 27 mi from Mancos: a \"Family-run ranch offering 17 shepherd wagon sites and camping, established 1965.\""},{"name":"Kokopelli Bike and Board","source":"https://www.kokopellibike.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"own website rental booking or walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"130 W Main St, Cortez ((970) 565-4408) and 315 Central Ave, Dolores ((970) 676-0060): \"Shop Local!\" - bikes and gear for sale, with rentals at both locations, and access to Phil''s World, Sand Canyon and High Country trails."},{"name":"WildEdge Brewing Collective","source":"https://www.wildedgebrewing.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"111 North Market, Cortez: \"opened on April 11th, 2017 in downtown Cortez after a 7 month renovation of a vacant warehouse\"; Tue-Sat 3-9 pm, Sun 3-7 pm, closed Mondays."},{"name":"Mancos Brewing Company","source":"https://www.mancosbrewingcompany.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"484 Hwy 160 E Frontage Rd, Mancos: \"a true public house\"; \"We offer wood fired pizza, fresh salads, sandwiched, home style casserole dishes and appetizers\"; closed Tuesdays."},{"name":"Dolores River Brewery","source":"https://www.doloresriverbrewery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","entertainment"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":42,"blurb":"100 S 4th St, Dolores: \"SW Colorado''s premium beer garden and music space\", \"SINCE 2002\"; wood-fired pizza Friday-Sunday and rotating food partners; open Tue-Sun from 4 pm; 970-882-4677."},{"name":"The Pie Maker Bakery","source":"https://mesaverdecountry.com/directory/the-pie-maker-bakery/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":43,"blurb":"Listed by Mesa Verde Country at \"17 North Harrison Street, Cortez, CO 81321\", \"(970) 560-6039\"; its own site redirects to a Square store that did not render."},{"name":"The Depot","source":"https://mesaverdecountry.com/directory/the-depot/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":44,"blurb":"Listed by Mesa Verde Country under Specialty & Farm-to-Table at \"520 Railroad Ave., Dolores, CO, 81323\", (970) 882-7500."},{"name":"Cortez","source":"https://mesaverdecountry.com/directory_category/hotels-motels/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":45,"blurb":"The western gateway: Mesa Verde Country lists its Holiday Inn Express, Hampton Inn and Best Western, RV parks on East Main Street, WildEdge Brewing and The Pie Maker Bakery; the park is a \"one-hour drive from Cortez\" (NPS)."},{"name":"Mancos","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/d/united-states/colorado/mancos/camping/glamping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","glamping"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":46,"blurb":"The eastern gateway on Highway 160: Mesa Verde RV Resort, Mancos Brewing Company, Mancos State Park and the glamping listings Hipcamp measures from it; NPS names Mancos as a pet-boarding community."},{"name":"Dolores","source":"https://mesaverdecountry.com/directory_category/rv-parks-campgrounds/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - a town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":47,"blurb":"Mesa Verde Country''s third community, north of Cortez: Dolores River Brewery, The Depot on Railroad Ave, a Kokopelli Bike and Board shop and the Dolores River RV Resort."}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you need reservations for Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"Not to enter: \"Mesa Verde National Park is Open Daily, Year-Round\" with no reservations required. The ranger-led cliff dwelling tours do need tickets: \"Reservations open 14 days in advance, beginning at 8:00 am MDT and fill up early.\" Step House needs no reservation.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/cliff_dwelling_tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What tours are there at Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"Ranger-led tours of Cliff Palace (\"45-minute\", four ladders), Balcony House (\"one-hour\", a 32 ft ladder and a tunnel), Long House (\"90-minute\", 2.25 miles), and the backcountry Square Tower House, Mug House and Oak Tree House tours (\"120-minute\"). Step House is self-guided.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/cliff_dwelling_tours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Mesa Verde National Park free?","a":"No. A private vehicle is $30.00 from May 1 to Oct 22, \"Valid for 7 days\", and $20.00 from Oct 23 to Apr 30; per person $15.00. \"This park does not accept cash\" - \"Entrance fees are credit/debit only.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Mesa Verde National Park open year round?","a":"Yes: \"Mesa Verde National Park is Open Daily, Year-Round.\" In winter Far View Lodge, Morefield Campground and most dining close, while the Mesa Top Loop Road stays open; cliff dwelling tours \"Begin in early May\" and end mid-to-late October.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"How long do you need at Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"The NPS says to plan \"at least two hours just to drive into and out of the park\" - the first cliff dwelling viewpoint is 21 miles, about 45 minutes, up the park road. A Long House visit alone takes \"115 minutes to 135 minutes\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp in Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"Yes, at Morefield Campground, \"located four miles from the park entrance. It has spaces for tents, trailers, and RVs, including 15 full-hookup RV sites (reservations recommended).\" It is operated by Aramark.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/eatingsleeping.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you stay in Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"\"Far View Lodge is the only lodging located within Mesa Verde National Park\", 15 miles beyond the entrance, with 150 Kiva and Kiva Deluxe View rooms and \"no in-room televisions or cell service\".","source":"https://www.visitmesaverde.com/stay/far-view-lodge","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you take dogs to Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"Only in limited places: \"Leashed pets are allowed on roads, parking lots, and paved areas on Mesa Top Loop and Park Point\", but \"not on trails, in ancestral sites or buildings\". \"A kennel is available in the Morefield Campground\" (970-565-2133).","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to Mesa Verde National Park?","a":"The NPS lists airports at Cortez, Colorado; Durango, Colorado; and Farmington, New Mexico. The park is a \"one-hour drive from Cortez\" and a \"1.5 hour drive from Durango\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When was Mesa Verde National Park established?","a":"\"President Theodore Roosevelt established Mesa Verde National Park on June 29, 1906\", \"the first national park of its kind\", to preserve \"nearly 5,000 ancestral sites\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/meve/learn/historyculture/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mesa Verde National Park: Cliff Dwelling Tours, Far View Lodge & Where to Stay | TravelWell","meta_description":"Ranger-led Cliff Palace and Balcony House tours, booked 14 days ahead, Far View Lodge, Morefield Campground and stays in Cortez and Mancos.","slug":"mesa-verde-national-park-colorado","primary_keyword":"Mesa Verde National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Mesa Verde National Park Cliff Palace"}}'::jsonb, 81),
  ('great-sand-dunes-colorado', '12A', 'Great Sand Dunes National Park', 'United States', 'Tallest dunes in North America', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'The Colorado Rockies', '{"hiking","adventure","family","wildlife","parks"}', '{"dramatic","wild","adventurous","remote"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"High Dune on First Ridge","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/hiking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - covered by the park entrance pass","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"\"the most common destination in the dunefield, providing a great view of the entire dunefield. It is about 688 feet (209 m) from base to top.\" \"Average round trip hiking time for High Dune is 2 hours over 2.5 miles (4 km)\" - but \"Plan to take as much as 4 hours to hike roundtrip, if not acclimated to the higher elevation\". There are no trails in the dunefield."},{"name":"Sandboarding and sand sledding on the dunefield","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/sandboardingsandsledding.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","group"],"booking_route":"none needed in the park - boards are rented from San Luis Valley shops before arrival","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"Sandboarding, sledding, and skiing are permitted anywhere on the dunefield away from vegetated areas.\" From the main Dunes Parking Area \"it''s a minimum 0.7 mile (1km) hike to get to the small or medium-sized slopes; the top of the first high ridge is 1.25 miles.\" \"The National Park Service does not rent sand sleds or sandboards. Plan to rent gear before arriving at the park.\""},{"name":"Medano Creek and its surge flow","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/medano-creek.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - covered by the park entrance pass","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"When there''s water in Medano Creek at the base of the dunes, adults and kids alike love to splash in the stream. Watch for waves in the water, a phenomenon called ''surge flow.''\" Peak flow \"in an average year occurs in late May or early June\". ⚠️ 2026: \"Snow pack in the Medano Creek watershed in the Sangre de Cristo Mountains is at near record low for this year.\""},{"name":"Hidden Dune","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/hiking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - covered by the park entrance pass","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"Hidden Dune is the tallest dune in North America at 741 feet (225 m).\" \"Plan on 7 miles (11 km) round trip over 6 hours, starting from the main Dunes Parking Lot\"; \"A false summit... hides the actual summit for much of the hike\"."},{"name":"Star Dune","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/hiking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - covered by the park entrance pass","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"currently the second tallest dune in North America. It is a majestic dune now measuring 736 feet (224 m) from base to summit.\" \"From the Dunes Parking Lot, hike about 2 miles (3.2 km) south down the Medano Creek bed until the massive pyramid-shaped Star Dune comes into view. Follow a ridge to its summit.\""},{"name":"Pinon Flats Campground","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/pinonflatscampground.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","group","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or 1-877-444-6777 (reservation only)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"\"located one mile north of the Visitor Center, open April through October. All sites are by reservation\"; individual sites \"$20/night\", \"88 sites, tents and/or RVs up to 25 feet (no hook-ups available)\"; a few driveways fit RVs to 35 feet; restrooms with flush toilets and potable water in all three loops, no showers; \"Each site has a bear locker\". Group sites A and B (20-40 people, $80) and C (15-30 people, $65), tents only."},{"name":"Dunes Backcountry and Sand Ramp Trail backpacking","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/backpacking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov permit ($6.00 non-refundable)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"\"Great Sand Dunes National Park offers two different backpacking experiences - seven designated sites along the Sand Ramp Trail and 20 non-designated sites in the Dunes Backcountry.\" Permits \"are only available through the Recreation.gov online permit system for a non-refundable fee of $6.00\"; \"No Permits are required for backpacking in the Great Sand Dunes National Preserve.\" Buck Creek, 1.0 mile from the Amphitheater lot, is \"ideal for families with children who want a short backpacking hike\"."},{"name":"Medano Pass Primitive Road","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/medano-pass-road.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","motoring","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - own high-clearance 4WD, or a 4WD tour/rental from the operators the NPS lists","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities","move"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"4-Wheel Drive (4WD) high-clearance vehicles with a 4L transfer case setting ARE REQUIRED on this road. All-Wheel-Drive (AWD) vehicles, mini-SUVs, wagons, and similar vehicles with lower clearance are not permitted\"; \"there is no cellular signal along the Medano Pass Primitive Road\". Conditions as of October 2nd, 2026: OPEN, with \"difficult and deep water conditions at the 3rd, 4th, and 5th Creek Crossings.\" Camping \"in one of 21 sites\" first-come, first-served when open."},{"name":"International Dark Sky Park nights","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/experiencethenight.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","romance","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - the park is open 24 hours","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"Half the park is after dark! With a combination of dry air, little light pollution, and high elevation, Great Sand Dunes National Park and Preserve is certified as an International Dark Sky Park by Dark Sky International\"; view \"at least 1 1/2 hours after sunset, or 1 1/2 hours before sunrise\"; \"August and September provide some of the best night skies of the year\"."},{"name":"Great Sand Dunes Junior Ranger programme","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/learn/kidsyouth/junior-ranger.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"none needed - pick up the booklet at the Visitor Center","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"\"plan on a total visit of at least 2 hours to complete the Junior Ranger Booklet, available at the visitor center. There are three different age groups in the booklet: 3-6, 7-9, 10-12, and 13 and up.\" Completers \"earn a Great Sand Dunes Junior Ranger Badge\"; the booklet can be downloaded before the visit."},{"name":"Free dunes sand wheelchairs","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","family"],"booking_route":"phone reservation with the Visitor Center, 719-378-6395 (free loan)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"Visitors can reserve the free use of special balloon-tire wheelchairs to access the dunes. You''ll need a strong helper to push the chair through sand.\" A 4-wheel or 3-wheel chair; leave an ID at the Visitor Center; \"Reserve a wheelchair in advance by calling the visitor center at 719-378-6395.\" One chair \"has been provided by Friends of the Dunes.\""},{"name":"Great Sand Dunes Visitor Center","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/visitor-center.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"none needed - 11999 State Highway 150, Mosca, CO 81146; (719) 378-6395","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"\"Rangers are present to assist you with trip planning, Junior Ranger books and badges, directions, and other questions\"; exhibits include \"a large diorama depicting park and preserve ecosystems, a night sky video\" and \"a 3D model of the valley\"; a 20-minute park video. Open daily 9:00 am - 4:30 pm \"except Thanksgiving, Christmas, and New Year''s Day\" (2025 hours as posted)."},{"name":"Horseback riding in the park and preserve","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/horse-and-pack-animal-use.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed for day rides; backcountry stock camping by permit","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"Most of the national park and the entire national preserve are open to horse use\"; trailers park at \"the horse trailer parking area at the beginning of the Medano Pass Primitive Road\"; horses may camp at the Little Medano, Aspen, Cold Creek and Sand Creek backcountry sites with a permit. Pinon Flats, the Dunes Parking Lot area to High Dune and the Wellington Ditch Trail are closed to horses."},{"name":"Closed-toe boots for 150-degree sand","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/hiking.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"NPS: \"High-top boots with long pants work best to keep sand out of your shoes. Do not wear sandals, which will just chafe your feet. If you must hike on a summer afternoon, bring closed-toe boots or shoes to prevent burning your feet.\" And: \"Keep your close-toed shoes/boots with you while riding boards so that you can walk on hot sand before and after riding.\""},{"name":"Sun hat, sunscreen, layers and wind goggles","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/conditions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"NPS ranger tips: \"Protect yourself from the cold and sun with sunscreen, sunglasses, and DRINK plenty of water. The air is usually very dry in this high elevation semi-desert environment.\" \"Wear Layered Clothing - Be prepared for chilly nights and sunny cool to warm days, windy conditions\"; \"Goggles can be a handy item during higher wind days.\""},{"name":"Dunes backpacking kit: sand stakes and a gallon of water a night","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/permitcontent/4675316","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to campsaver.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"The park''s Recreation.gov permit page: \"Backpackers must carry 1 gallon of water/person/night as there is no creek to filter\"; \"Secure tents with sand stakes or sandbags. Strong winds may occur any time of year.\" \"Sand temperatures may reach 150° F on summer afternoons. Wear closed-toe shoes\"."},{"name":"Great Dunes Oasis Board Shop","source":"https://www.greatdunes.com/ride/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in only - \"No apps, no online booking\"; 719-378-2222","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"Named by the NPS as \"located 4 miles from the Great Sand Dunes Visitor Center near the park entrance\". Its own page: \"Sand Board : $20 / day (+ tax) Sand Sled: $20 / day (+ tax)\"; \"No reservations needed. Just stop by the board shop during open hours\"; \"Daily Rentals are due back by 3:30 pm\". Board Shop 9a-4p."},{"name":"Great Sand Dunes Oasis campground and motel","source":"https://www.greatdunes.com/stays/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family","group"],"booking_route":"phone only - 719-378-2222 (\"No apps, no online booking\")","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"The last stop before the tallest sand dunes in North America. Store, restaurant, R.V. spaces, rooms, cabins, tent sites, and board rentals; just minutes away from the park entrance.\" Wilderness tent sites $33 (first-come, first-served), 20 full-hookup pull-thru RV sites at $55, rustic cabins $88, motel $219 (open 5/1 to 9/30), four group tent sites for 10-75 people. \"Just our family serving yours since 1985.\""},{"name":"Rustic Rook Resort","source":"https://rusticrookresort.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","romance"],"booking_route":"own website \"Book Now\" or (719) 270-1356","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"\"Choose from Fully Furnished Glamping Tents, Grain Bin Villas, Camper Cabins and BYO Tent Sites\"; \"located just 19 miles from the Great Sand Dunes National Park entrance\"; \"enjoy a complimentary hot breakfast each morning and S''mores by the campfire at night\"; sled rental and an International Dark Skies page. \"Grain Bins open year around | All other sites open May 18th 2026 - Oct 3rd\"."},{"name":"Zapata Falls Campground and Recreation Area","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/261715","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure","group"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (the NPS: \"Zapata Falls Campground is now by reservation on recreation.gov\")","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","activities"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"BLM / Colorado State Land Board area \"approximately 5 miles south of Great Sand Dunes National Park and Preserve\", campground \"3.5 miles (5.8km) up an unpaved road. Elevation 9,088ft.\" \"23 Individual sites (11 Tent, 12 RV, 1 Group Tent...)\", vault toilets, \"No public drinking water system\", \"no hookup services\". The trail to the falls is \"rocky and steep\" - wading the creek \"is the only way to reach the falls.\""},{"name":"Base Camp Family Campground and RV Park","source":"https://www.basecampfamilycampground.com/home","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"own website \"BOOK ONLINE\"; 719-589-2938","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","gear"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"\"Voted #1 Campground in Alamosa Colorado\": \"Largest Pull Through Sites In The Area-100'' x 40''\", \"Big-Rig-Friendly\", full hookups, huge tent sites with a 10x10 shelter, dry cabins (\"Electric Only - Bring Your Own Bedding\"), large private showers, laundry, and \"Sand Board & Sand Sled Rentals (Site Delivery Available)\"."},{"name":"Cool Sunshine RV Park","source":"https://www.coolsunshinervpark.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","senior"],"booking_route":"own website \"Check Availability\" / \"Book Your Stay\"; 719-992-9105","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"\"a pet-friendly RV park with 41 camp sites (full hookup back-in sites and pull through sites) and 6 tent sites\", \"just a block from downtown\" Alamosa, with a clubhouse and a covered patio with putting green; \"over 30 restaurants within a 15 minute walk\"."},{"name":"Alamosa / Great Sand Dunes KOA Journey","source":"https://koa.com/campgrounds/alamosa/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"koa.com \"Book Now\" or 1-719-589-9757","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"A KOA Journey campground: \"Pull-through RV Sites with 50-amp service\", \"Premium Tent Sites\" and lodging; \"Panoramic Mountain Views\". The NPS lists it \"31 miles southwest of Great Sand Dunes Visitor Center, 4 miles east of Alamosa. RVs, hookups, tents, cabins. Open warmer months only.\""},{"name":"Hampton Inn Alamosa","source":"https://alamosa.org/blog/listing_categories/hotels-motels","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"Listed by Visit Alamosa: \"Hampton Inn Alamosa combines modern comforts with small-town hospitality, offering a convenient home base near downtown Alamosa, Great Sand Dunes National Park, and the best of the San Luis Valley.\" The brand page was not fetched (hilton.com routinely refuses), so nothing else is stated here."},{"name":"Fairfield Inn & Suites Alamosa","source":"https://alamosa.org/blog/listing_categories/hotels-motels","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"Listed by Visit Alamosa: \"Located on the west side of Alamosa near shopping, entertainment, and local attractions, Fairfield Inn & Suites offers a comfortable stay with modern amenities and easy access to Great Sand Dunes National Park and Adams State University.\" The brand page was not fetched (marriott.com routinely refuses)."},{"name":"Holiday Inn Express Hotel & Suites Alamosa","source":"https://www.americansouthwest.net/colorado/hotels/alamosa.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"Listed by American Southwest at \"3418 Mariposa Street, Alamosa, CO 81101\": \"74 rooms and suites\", \"an indoor pool, (small) fitness center, whirlpool and free breakfast bar\"; \"the Great Sand Dunes, is 33 miles away.\" The guide carries affiliate links (its own disclosure); the IHG page was not fetched."},{"name":"Kristi Mountain Sports","source":"https://www.kristimountainsports.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in or phone 719-589-9759","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","shop"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"\"Since 1969, Kristi Mountain Sports has been the San Luis Valley''s premier location for all your biking, hiking, camping, climbing, skiing, snowboarding, and sandboarding needs\"; \"Sandboard & Sled Rentals $20/day\"; \"Walk-in''s welcome!\" The NPS: rents \"year round. Call (719) 589-9759 the day before to reserve a board... Closed Tuesdays and Wednesdays.\""},{"name":"Spindrift Sandboards","source":"https://www.spindriftsandboards.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"own website \"Reserve Your Board\"; (719) 379-4410","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"\"Located just 25 miles from Great Sand Dunes National Park and Preserve, Spindrift Sandboards offers the premier sandboarding and sandsledding experience in Blanca, Colorado\"; \"Rentals start at $20 per board or sled per day, plus tax\"; \"Instruction available for new riders\"; \"After-hours drop-off available upon request\"."},{"name":"Dunes 4x4 Ltd","source":"https://www.dunes4x4.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","motoring","senior"],"booking_route":"call or email to schedule; 303-564-7705","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","move"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"Half-day 4x4 adventure tours: \"travel along the Medano Pass 4x4 road, winding along the edge of the dune field and up into the Sangre de Cristo mountains\"; \"We provide beverages and snacks along the way, stretch our legs and hike in the creek, into the dunes, and there is opportunity for sand boarding too.\" Listed by the NPS for 4WD tours, 303-564-7705."},{"name":"Kaiyote Tours","source":"https://www.kaiyotetours.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","group","adventure"],"booking_route":"own website Reservations page; 970-556-6103","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"guide","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"Its own site lists \"Sand Dunes N.P.\" tours in \"Birding\", \"Hiking\" and \"Overnight Backpacking\", alongside Rocky Mountain N.P. \"Family and Group Tours\". The NPS: \"This company offers guided birding, hiking, or overnight backpacking tours of Great Sand Dunes National Park and Preserve. 970-556-6103.\""},{"name":"Great Sand Dunes Oasis Restaurant","source":"https://www.greatdunes.com/eat/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; 719-378-2222","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"\"Hot meals, cold drinks, and a view of the dunes. Breakfast, lunch, and dinner\" - breakfast burritos \"smothered with your choice of secret family recipe red or green chili\", huevos rancheros, a kids'' menu; \"Groups of 6 or more add 18% gratuity\". ⚠️ The home page on 2026-10-03 read \"Restaurant: Closed for the Season\"."},{"name":"Dune Valley Distillery","source":"https://www.dunevalleydistillery.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","adventure","group"],"booking_route":"own website - board rental appointments and event tickets; email for private tastings","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","gear"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"\"Producing unique Colorado vodkas made from local Potato and Quinoa\"; \"BOARDS BOTTLES & BEBIDAS and small bites\", sandboard rentals, an event and music venue; \"We are about 15 miles north of Alamosa and a stones throw away from the Great Sand Dunes\". September 2026 hours Thursday-Saturday 11am-8pm, Tuesday & Wednesday 11am-5pm."},{"name":"San Luis Valley Brewing Company","source":"https://www.slvbrewco.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","group"],"booking_route":"walk-in or order online; (719) 587-2337","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"631 Main Street, Alamosa: \"OPEN 7 DAYS A WEEK!\", 11am-10pm daily; year-round beers include Alamosa Amber, Ol'' 169 Oatmeal Stout and the chili beer Valle Caliente; \"we seek out the highest quality ingredients to ensure our beer has the full flavor and excellence that define a great small-batch craft brewery.\""},{"name":"Calvillo''s Mexican Restaurant","source":"https://www.alamosa.org/listing/calvillos-mexican-restaurant/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","group","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; banquet room by phone (719) 587-5500","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Visit Alamosa: \"dedicated to serving authentic Mexican cuisine, offering a diverse menu that highlights the rich culinary traditions and regional dishes from various states across Mexico\"; \"an all-day buffet\", a full bar and \"a banquet room, making it suitable for both casual dining and hosting larger group events\". 400 Main Street, (719) 587-5500."},{"name":"Milagros Coffeehouse","source":"https://alamosa.org/?p=2414","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"walk-in; 719-589-9299","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"Visit Alamosa: \"a 501(c)3 nonprofit and a social enterprise of La Puente\" serving \"simple, healthy, delicious food and beverages\"; \"All proceeds go to support the social services of La Puente.\" 529 Main Street, 719-589-9299."},{"name":"Sand Dunes Recreation hot springs pool","source":"http://www.sanddunespool.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wellness","family","senior"],"booking_route":"own website (admission and lodging pages); 719-378-2807","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities","stay","eat"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"\"Natural Hot artesian Oasis\" north of Hooper, with \"Cabins, RV & Tent Sites\", The Greenhouse, the Mile Deep Grille \"located near main pool\" and the Pivot Public House; \"ENTIRE FACILITY IS CLOSED EVERY THURSDAY FOR CLEANING\". The NPS lists it as \"privately owned facility located 32 miles west\" with a \"geothermal swimming pool\", open year round, and it rents sandsleds and sandboards."},{"name":"Mile Deep Grille at Sand Dunes Recreation","source":"https://www.sanddunespool.com/eat-drink","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in at the facility","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"The hot-springs facility''s restaurant, \"located near main pool\", with a small-plates menu in The Greenhouse; the facility is closed every Thursday. Menu and hours were not published on the page read."},{"name":"Colorado Gators Reptile Rescue","source":"https://coloradogators.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","wildlife"],"booking_route":"pay at the gate; (719) 378-2612","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"\"See hundreds of rescued reptiles including alligators, crocodiles, caiman, tortoises, and turtles\"; \"All visitors to Colorado Gators have the opportunity to pet, hold, and take pictures with a small alligator!\" 2026: open daily 9am-5pm February 27 - November 01. Admission: 5 and under free, 6-15 $15, 16-64 $30, \"Ages 65-79 $15\", 80 and over free. 9162 Lane 9 N, Mosca."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Great Sand Dunes National Park free?","a":"No. The NPS lists \"Private Vehicle: $25.00\", \"Motorcycle: $20.00\" and \"Per Person: $15.00\" for visitors 16 or older (children under 16 enter free), or \"Annual Entrance - Park: $45.00\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need reservations for Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"Not to enter: \"There are no advance reservations, timed entries, or visitor limits at Great Sand Dunes. It is optional to purchase your entrance pass in advance.\" Camping at Pinon Flats is by reservation only on Recreation.gov.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes. Pinon Flats Campground is \"open April through October. All sites are by reservation on recreation.gov or call 1-877-444-6777. Individual and group sites can be reserved up to 3 months in advance.\" Backpackers camp in the Dunes Backcountry or at Sand Ramp Trail sites with a $6.00 Recreation.gov permit.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/pinonflatscampground.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you sandboard at Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes: \"Sandboarding, sledding, and skiing are permitted anywhere on the dunefield away from vegetated areas.\" But \"The National Park Service does not rent sand sleds or sandboards. Plan to rent gear before arriving at the park.\" The nearest listed rental is the Great Dunes Oasis Store, 4 miles from the Visitor Center.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/sandboardingsandsledding.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need 4WD for Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"Not for the main park area - Highway 150 and County Road 6 \"are paved highways\". Only the Medano Pass Primitive Road needs it: \"4-Wheel Drive (4WD) high-clearance vehicles with a 4L transfer case setting ARE REQUIRED on this road.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/medano-pass-road.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you ride ATVs at Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"No: \"Mechanized or motorized vehicles are not permitted on the dunefield, and ATVs are not permitted in the park and preserve.\" The dunes \"were made a wilderness by Congress in 1976\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/faqs.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"Yes, on a leash of 6 feet or less, in the main use areas: \"Pets are permitted in the Preserve (including Mosca Pass Trail) and main use areas of the Park (including Pinon Flats Campground, Dunes Overlook Trail, and along the Medano Pass Primitive Road).\" They are not permitted \"In the backcountry of the dunefield, beyond the first high ridge of dunes\". The NPS warns of sand \"up to 150 degrees F\" and suggests pet booties.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the closest airport to Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"\"Commercial air service is available to a small airport at Alamosa, Colorado, 38 miles from Great Sand Dunes. Colorado Springs, Denver, and Albuquerque are served by many commercial airlines. Rental cars are available at all these airports.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the best time to visit Great Sand Dunes National Park?","a":"It depends on what you come for. \"September has some of the best weather of the year, with an average high of 71 F and a low of 42 F.\" For the creek, \"Late May and early June are the best opportunity to experience ''surge flow''\" - but those weekends \"are extremely crowded\". In summer, \"always plan your dunes time for early morning or evening\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/conditions-to-expect.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When is Great Sand Dunes National Park open?","a":"\"Great Sand Dunes National Park and Preserve is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, year round.\" The Visitor Center was posted as open \"daily 9:00 am - 4:30 pm throughout the year, except Thanksgiving, Christmas, and New Year''s Day\" (2025 hours); Pinon Flats Campground is open April through October.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/grsa/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Sand Dunes National Park: Dunes, Sandboarding & Camping | TravelWell","meta_description":"North America''s tallest dunes: High Dune and Star Dune hikes, sandboard rentals nearby, Pinon Flats camping booked 3 months out, and dark-sky nights.","slug":"great-sand-dunes-national-park-colorado","primary_keyword":"Great Sand Dunes National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Great Sand Dunes National Park dunes Sangre de Cristo"}}'::jsonb, 82)
